                <pb facs="1227" n="1095" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg1095"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.6363/60: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-01-30T15:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 30,
                                1926—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 30—5:42
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>59. American consul at Swatow telegraphs that Swatow authorities have instituted
                    oil monopoly similar to that in operation at Canton—see Canton’s despatch 366,
                    October 27th, to Department.<anchor n="92" xml:id="d846-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
